{"id":"0ecb6479-1f23-443e-8601-40a32f17608c","object":"chat.completion","created":1784824712,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\"implementation\":\"def solve(case):\\n    segments = case['segments']\\n    budget = case['budget']\\n    # Validate: each segment must have required fields\\n    segs = []\\n    for i, s in enumerate(segments):\\n        name = s.get('name')\\n        imp = s.get('importance')\\n        min_q = s.get('minimum')\\n        cap = s.get('capacity')\\n        if None in (name, imp, min_q, cap):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"Missing segment fields\\\")\\n        if not isinstance(imp, (int, float)) or imp < 0:\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"Importance must be non-negative number\\\")\\n        if not isinstance(min_q, int) or not isinstance(cap, int):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"Minimum and capacity must be integers\\\")\\n        if min_q < 0 or cap < min_q:\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"Invalid minimum or capacity\\\")\\n        segs.append({'name': name, 'importance': imp, 'minimum': min_q, 'capacity': cap, 'index': i})\\n    sum_min = sum(s['minimum'] for s in segs)\\n    sum_cap = sum(s['capacity'] for s in segs)\\n    if budget < sum_min or budget > sum_cap:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Budget out of feasible range\\\")\\n    alloc = {s['name']: s['minimum'] for s in segs}\\n    remaining = budget - sum_min\\n    while remaining > 0:\\n        best_idx = None\\n        best_num = 0\\n        best_den = 1\\n        for s in segs:\\n            name = s['name']\\n            cur = alloc[name]\\n            if cur >= s['capacity']:\\n                continue\\n            num = s['importance']\\n            den = cur + 1\\n            if best_idx is None or num * best_den > best_num * den:\\n                best_idx = s['index']\\n                best_num = num\\n                best_den = den\\n            elif num * best_den == best_num * den and s['index'] < best_idx:\\n                best_idx = s['index']\\n        if best_idx is None:\\n            break\\n        name = segs[best_idx]['name']\\n        alloc[name] += 1\\n        remaining -= 1\\n    total = sum(alloc.values())\\n    name_mapping = [s['name'] for s in segs]\\n    return {\\n        'allocations': alloc,\\n        'name_mapping': name_mapping,\\n        'total_allocated': total\\n    }\"}","reasoning_content":"We need to implement solve(case) that returns a JSON-serializable object. The task: allocate budget across segments with minimum quotas, capacities, importance scores. The algorithm: start all at minimum, then while budget remains (after subtracting sum of minima), allocate one token to segment that maximizes importance / (next allocated position + 1?) Actually \"importance divided by its next allocated position\". Since we start at minimum, the next allocated position for a segment is its current allocation+1 (the position index starting from 1?). Typically in such problems, we allocate sequentially, each new token to segment with highest importance/(current_allocation+1) or something like that. But careful: \"importance divided by its next allocated position\". If segment has minimum m, then after minimum, next token would be allocation = m+1, so ratio = importance/(m+1). Then after that, next ratio = importance/(m+2), etc. That's typical for greedy allocation with harmonic series. But we also have capacity. So we allocate one token at a time to the segment with highest ratio, but only if it hasn't reached capacity. If multiple have same ratio, break ties by original segment order (list order). Continue until budget exhausted or all at capacity. Return allocations as dict mapping name to allocated amount (including minimum). Also need name mapping? The spec says \"Return allocations, the name mapping, and the conserved total.\" The output should have keys: allocations (dict name->int), total_allocated (int), maybe something else? The case has 